  "id": "reinforcement-delay",
  "term": "reinforcement delay",
  "definition": "Reinforcement delay is a schedule condition in which the reinforcing event is not immediate but occurs after a set wait, such as 300 or 600 seconds instead of 0 seconds. In the supplied study, these delays were associated with longer gaps between visits and changes in response rate.",
